    "result_text": "Tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI agree with both findings and addressed them:\n\n**Finding 1 (layering leak) \u2014 fixed.** Removed `getSelfLink()` from the `Owner` JPA entity. The URL path is a REST transport concern, not an intrinsic domain derivation like `getIdentityKey`/`getAgeBand`, so it no longer lives in the persistence model.\n\n**Finding 2 (duplicated literal) \u2014 fixed.** The `selfLink` is now computed in the web layer via an `@AfterMapping` hook on `OwnerMapper`, and the `/api/owners/{id}` template exists exactly once as `OwnerMapper.OWNER_PATH_TEMPLATE`, referenced both by the derived `selfLink` and the controller's `Location` header \u2014 so the two can't drift.\n\nPlacing it in the mapper (rather than scattering it across the controller's four DTO-returning methods) means every `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` conversion \u2014 single, collection, and page \u2014 gets `selfLink` from one definition, and it stays null until the owner has an id, matching the OpenAPI contract.\n\nThe `openapi.yml` addition stayed as-is, as the review noted. The acceptance test `coreReturnsSelfLink` still passes.",
